    <title>Past Medical History</title>
    <text><paragraph>Historical biography with true dates. These events are not part of the synthetic care timeline.</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Historical date</th><th>History</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>June 23, 1940</td><td>Born prematurely, weighing about 4.5 pounds</td><td>D (CLM-0002)</td></tr><tr><td>about 1944</td><td>Double pneumonia followed by scarlet fever at about age four, among other childhood illnesses</td><td>D (CLM-0003)</td></tr><tr><td>about 1945</td><td>Poliomyelitis in early childhood, leaving the left leg paralyzed or partly paralyzed, with the foot turned inward</td><td>D (CLM-0004)</td></tr><tr><td>about 1946</td><td>Metal leg brace and special shoe for several years; weekly treatment at Meharry Medical College in Nashville, with massage and heat, and massage at home several times a day</td><td>D (CLM-0005)</td></tr><tr><td>about 1952</td><td>Walking without the brace by about age 12; later an Olympic sprinter</td><td>D (CLM-0006, CLM-0007)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

