<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Vice president of a Nashville hospital; former Olympic champion sprinter, teacher and coach; runs a foundation that supports young track and field athletes [S]</item><item>Lives in a suburb of Nashville; four grown children and a very large extended family nearby, and many friends from track and field [S]</item><item>Remembers being told as a child that she would never walk again; wants to be told plainly what is happening and to stay as independent and active as she can [S]</item><item>Never smoker; alcohol rarely; no drug use [S]</item><item>Walks for exercise most days; drives herself to work [S]</item><item>Menstrual history: periods stopped about two years ago; no hormone therapy [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

